  "final_message": "I haven't made any changes. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` would break a deployed consumer.\n\n`contracts/consumers/analytics-ingest__OrderPlaced.json` lists `channel` (`enum:web|store|marketplace`) under `requires`. That contract is pinned to `deployedVersion: 3`, so analytics-ingest is live and still depends on the field. Nothing in orders-service reads `channel`, but that doesn't mean the downstream consumers don't. `npm run` has no script for contract checks, but `scripts/verify-contracts.mjs` appears to check these contracts, and it would fail too.\n\nThere are three ways to go:\n\n1. **Remove it from the order model only.** Drop `channel` from `Order`, `NewOrder`, request parsing and validation, but keep it on the `OrderPlaced` event. The event would need another source for the value, such as the incoming request, so this only works if the order model can still carry it at placement time. That makes it only a partial removal.\n2. **Remove it everywhere, after analytics-ingest changes.** The analytics-ingest team stops requiring `channel` and deploys. Then I update their contract file and remove the field from the event, the model, parsing, validation, tests, `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, and `scripts/verify-contracts.mjs`. The `POST /orders` input shape changes too, so API clients would also be affected.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now.** I'd do this only if you confirm analytics-ingest no longer needs the field and the contract file is simply stale. I'd update the contract file as part of the change.\n\nWhich one do you want?",
